# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/expansion_social.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event soc_lost_notes
# en: The Borrowed Notes
title [f46501] = 借走的笔记
# en: {npc} borrowed your Lore notes last week. {They} {are} now standing in front of you holding a single soggy page. "There was a stream," {they} say{s}. "And a duck. Mostly a duck."
text [5dbc83] = {npc}上星期借走了你的学识课笔记。现在{they}站在你面前，手里只剩一页湿透的纸。“有条小溪，”{they}说，“还有一只鸭子。主要是鸭子。”
# en: A student holding a single soggy page of notes, the rest of the stack floating away down a stream behind them.
scene [daf951] = 一名学生手里攥着一页湿透的笔记，身后剩下的那叠正顺着小溪漂走。
# en: Laugh it off
opt.left.label [29c02a] = 一笑了之
# en: You rewrite your notes from memory. {npc} brings you a cake every day for a week, by way of apology. The cakes are better than the notes were.
opt.left.say.1 [37846c] = 你凭记忆重写了笔记。{npc}一连一星期每天给你带一块蛋糕赔罪。蛋糕比笔记还好。
# en: Make {them} rewrite them
opt.right.label [53cd0f] = 让{them}重抄一份
# en: {npc} copies out forty pages from a friend's notes, grumbling. The new notes are neater than yours ever were.
opt.right.say.1 [a8c805] = {npc}一边抱怨一边从朋友那儿抄了四十页。新笔记比你自己写的还工整。

@event soc_birthday
# en: A Birthday
title [492d55] = 生日
# en: You find out — by accident — that it's {npc}'s birthday. {They} haven't told anyone. {They} {are} spending it in the library, alone, on purpose.
text [184bc7] = 你偶然发现今天是{npc}的生日。{they}谁也没告诉，正一个人待在图书馆里——故意的。
# en: A small cake with a single candle in a dark common room, a group of students crouched behind a sofa, a surprised face in the doorway.
scene [85796d] = 漆黑的公共休息室里一个插着一根蜡烛的小蛋糕，一群学生蹲在沙发后面，门口一张惊讶的脸。
# en: Organise a surprise
opt.left.label [c1b395] = 策划一场惊喜
# en: Seven people jump out from behind a sofa. {npc} screams, then laughs, then has to sit down. "How did you know?" You'll never tell.
opt.left.say.1 [7240f2] = 七个人从沙发后面跳出来。{npc}尖叫，然后大笑，然后不得不坐下。“你们怎么知道的？”你永远不会说。
# en: Join {them} in the library
opt.right.label [d7c810] = 去图书馆陪{them}
# en: You sit down opposite {them} with your own book. Neither of you says happy birthday. At midnight {they} slide{s} a biscuit across the table, and you both grin.
opt.right.say.1 [6d7231] = 你带着自己的书在{them}对面坐下。谁也没说生日快乐。午夜时，{they}把一块饼干推过桌面，你们相视一笑。

@event soc_bad_news
# en: Bad News From Home
title [9ab55c] = 家里来的坏消息
# en: {npc} is sitting on the stairs with a letter in {their} lap, not moving. {Their} grandmother is ill. The barge home takes two days. "I don't know whether to go," {they} say{s}.
text [c5229c] = {npc}坐在楼梯上，膝上放着一封信，一动不动。{their}祖母病了。坐驳船回家要两天。“我不知道该不该回去，”{they}说。
# en: A student sitting on a stone staircase with a crumpled letter, head bowed, a friend sitting down beside them.
scene [e888fc] = 一名学生坐在石阶上，手里攥着一封揉皱的信，低着头，一个朋友在旁边坐下。
# en: "Go. We'll cover your classes."
opt.left.label [6868e0] = “去吧，课我们帮你顶着。”
# en: {npc} catches the next barge. You take notes for two in every lesson. When {npc} comes back, {their} grandmother is better, and {they} hug{s} you on the landing.
opt.left.say.1 [551a90] = {npc}赶上了下一班驳船。你每节课都记两份笔记。{npc}回来时，{their}祖母好些了，{they}在楼梯平台上抱住了你。
# en: Just sit with {them}
opt.right.label [75d0fd] = 只是陪{them}坐着
# en: You sit there until the stairs move under you. You don't fix anything. That's not what {they} needed.
opt.right.say.1 [439080] = 你们一直坐到楼梯在身下挪动。你什么也没解决。那本来就不是{they}需要的。

@event soc_stargazing
# en: Counting Stars
title [559b85] = 数星星
# en: {npc} has dragged a blanket up to the roof. "There's a meteor shower," {they} say{s}. "Supposedly." There's room on the blanket for two, just about.
text [9f0616] = {npc}把一条毯子拖上了屋顶。“有流星雨，”{they}说，“据说。”毯子上刚好够两个人躺。
# en: Two students lying on their backs on a flat roof, close but not quite touching, a sky full of stars above.
scene [6f5d93] = 两名学生仰面躺在平屋顶上，挨得很近却又没碰到，头顶是满天繁星。
# en: Count meteors
opt.left.label [b22e25] = 数流星
# en: You count thirty-one. {npc} counts thirty-four and accuses you of not looking properly. You weren't, entirely.
opt.left.say.1 [4409c0] = 你数到三十一颗。{npc}数到三十四颗，指责你没认真看。你确实没完全在看。
# en: Talk about everything else
opt.right.label [a3c084] = 聊些别的一切
# en: You don't see a single meteor. You talk about home and fear and what you'd do if you could do anything. When you look up, the sky's gone grey with dawn.
opt.right.say.1 [88b087] = 你一颗流星也没看到。你们聊家乡、聊恐惧、聊如果什么都能做会去做什么。等你抬起头，天已经泛起了黎明的灰白。

@event soc_jealous_friend
# en: Jealousy
title [bace8d] = 嫉妒
# en: {npc} has been odd all week. Finally it comes out. "You've got all these new friends now. I just — I don't know where I fit anymore."
text [090680] = {npc}一整个星期都怪怪的。终于说出来了：“你现在有那么多新朋友了。我就是——不知道自己还算什么了。”
# en: A student standing alone at the edge of a laughing group, arms folded, watching someone else take what used to be their seat.
scene [560bd3] = 一名学生抱着胳膊独自站在一群欢笑的人边上，看着别人坐上了曾经属于自己的位置。
# en: Reassure {them}
opt.left.label [c0cad1] = 让{them}安心
# en: You tell {them} exactly where {they} fit: right here, first. {npc} rolls {their} eyes, but {they}'re smiling. The oddness is gone by dinner.
opt.left.say.1 [944299] = 你明明白白地告诉{them}：{they}的位置就在这里，排第一。{npc}翻了个白眼，但在笑。晚饭前那股别扭劲就没了。
# en: Tell {them} friendship isn't a contest
opt.right.label [147a3c] = 告诉{them}友情不是比赛
# en: You're right, technically. {npc} knows it. It still lands badly. It takes a few weeks for things to feel easy again.
opt.right.say.1 [1dcb8f] = 严格来说你是对的。{npc}也知道。但这话还是说得不太好听。过了好几个星期，你们之间才重新自在起来。

@event soc_teach_spell
# en: A Trick Worth Learning
title [8a5e67] = 值得一学的小把戏
# en: {npc} has a spell {they} invented — a little thing, half-useful, half-ridiculous — and wants to teach it to someone. "It makes your tea exactly the right temperature," {they} say{s}. "Forever."
text [1a48bd] = {npc}有一个自己发明的咒语——一个小东西，一半有用，一半荒唐——想教给别人。“它能让你的茶永远保持刚刚好的温度，”{they}说，“永远。”
# en: Two students in an empty classroom, one demonstrating a wand movement, the other copying it with a tiny spark of light.
scene [bfffc4] = 空教室里两名学生，一个在示范魔杖的动作，另一个跟着模仿，杖尖冒出一点小火花。
# en: Learn it properly
opt.left.label [9c42bb] = 认真学会
# en: It takes an hour. Your tea is now perfect, always. You'll use this spell more than anything you learn in class.
opt.left.say.1 [9f0fc3] = 花了一个钟头。你的茶现在永远是完美的。这个咒语你用得会比课上学的任何东西都多。
# en: The first attempt freezes your tea solid, and your eyebrows with it. The second works. Your eyebrows take a day to thaw.
opt.left.say.2 [1057e1] = 第一次尝试把你的茶冻成了冰坨，连眉毛也一起冻上了。第二次成功了。你的眉毛花了一天才解冻。
# en: Teach {them} one of yours in return
opt.right.label [a24082] = 也教{them}一个你的
# en: You trade spells like secrets. By midnight you've both got a new trick and an inside joke that will last three years.
opt.right.say.1 [42f01a] = 你们像交换秘密一样交换咒语。到午夜时，你们都多了一个新把戏，还有一个能笑上三年的内部笑话。

@event soc_secret_admirer
# en: A Secret Admirer
title [6041b8] = 神秘的仰慕者
# en: Folded notes keep appearing in your library books. Unsigned. They're funny, and a little nervous, and they know things about you that only someone paying attention would know. The handwriting looks familiar.
text [a4cea9] = 你的图书馆借书里不断出现折好的字条。没有署名。它们很有趣，有点紧张，而且知道一些只有一直留意你的人才会知道的事。那笔迹看着有点眼熟。
# en: A folded note tucked into a library book with a pressed flower, unsigned, the handwriting careful and slightly shaky.
scene [469c2b] = 一张夹在图书馆书里的折叠字条，附着一朵压花，没有署名，字迹小心又微微发抖。
# en: Leave a note back
opt.left.label [ad88dc] = 回一张字条
# en: You write back. The notes get longer. One day the last line just says: "It's {npc}. You knew, didn't you?" You did.
opt.left.say.1 [5ee7cc] = 你回了信。字条越写越长。有一天，最后一行只写着：“是{npc}。你早就知道了，对吧？”你确实知道。
# en: Stake out the library
opt.right.label [010099] = 在图书馆蹲守
# en: You catch {npc} red-handed, mid-tuck. {They} turn{s} the colour of a pyromancy exam. You both laugh until the librarian throws you out.
opt.right.say.1 [a59ad0] = 你当场抓住了正往书里塞字条的{npc}。{they}的脸红得像火焰术考试。你们俩笑到被图书管理员赶了出去。
# en: You wait three nights and catch nobody. On the fourth morning the note says: "Nice try."
opt.right.say.2 [ec1e48] = 你守了三个晚上，谁也没抓到。第四天早上，字条上写着：“想得美。”

@event soc_injured_friend
# en: Carried
title [c0fda1] = 背回来
# en: {npc} has twisted an ankle on the far side of the grounds, a long way from the infirmary, and it's getting dark. {They} {are} trying very hard to pretend it doesn't hurt.
text [f03529] = {npc}在校园的另一头扭伤了脚踝，离医务室很远，天也快黑了。{they}正非常努力地假装一点也不疼。
# en: A student carrying another piggyback across a muddy lawn, the injured one's ankle wrapped in a scarf.
scene [042d6a] = 一名学生背着另一名学生穿过泥泞的草坪，受伤那位的脚踝用围巾裹着。
# en: Carry {them} on your back
opt.left.label [374549] = 把{them}背回去
# en: It's a long way. {npc} narrates the whole journey like a horse race. By the time you reach the infirmary you're both laughing too hard to breathe.
opt.left.say.1 [6e8e08] = 路很长。{npc}一路像解说赛马一样解说着。等你们到医务室时，两个人都笑得喘不上气。
# en: Run for help
opt.right.label [689bdc] = 跑去找人帮忙
# en: You run for Sister Amaranth, who arrives with a floating stretcher and a lot of opinions. {npc} is fine. {They} send{s} you a thank-you sweet.
opt.right.say.1 [b2b6c2] = 你跑去找阿玛兰斯修女，她带着一副漂浮担架和一肚子意见赶来了。{npc}没事。{they}送了你一块谢礼糖。

@event soc_rival_decency
# en: An Unexpected Kindness
title [10ec52] = 意外的善意
# en: You drop your books in the rain, and the first person to stoop and help pick them up is {npc}. {They} hand{s} them back without a word, looking as surprised as you are.
text [76c0d9] = 你的书在雨里掉了一地，第一个弯腰帮你捡的人竟是{npc}。{they}一言不发地把书递还给你，看上去和你一样惊讶。
# en: A student picking up a rival's scattered books from a wet floor, the rival frozen mid-step, not sure what to say.
scene [b9f110] = 一名学生从湿漉漉的地上捡起对手散落的书，对手僵在半步之中，不知该说什么。
# en: Thank {them} properly
opt.left.label [023f60] = 好好谢谢{them}
# en: "Don't make it a thing," {npc} mutters. But the next day {they} nod{s} to you in the corridor. Something has thawed.
opt.left.say.1 [563f24] = “别弄得像回事似的，”{npc}嘟囔道。但第二天，{they}在走廊里冲你点了点头。有什么东西解冻了。
# en: Suspect a trick
opt.right.label [5792ea] = 怀疑这是个圈套
# en: You check the books for hexes. There aren't any. {npc} saw you checking. You'll both remember that.
opt.right.say.1 [e359de] = 你检查书上有没有恶咒。没有。{npc}看见你在检查。你们俩都会记住这件事。

@event soc_partner_anniversary
# en: An Anniversary
title [a63670] = 纪念日
# en: It's been a while now — long enough that {npc} has started calling things "ours". Today {they} hand{s} you a small wrapped box and won't meet your eyes.
text [7539ef] = 已经有一阵子了——久到{npc}开始把东西叫作“我们的”。今天{they}递给你一个包好的小盒子，不敢看你的眼睛。
# en: Two people on a bench by the lake at sunset, one holding out a small wrapped box, the other's hands over their mouth.
scene [3c4e6d] = 日落时分，两个人坐在湖边的长椅上，一个递出一个包好的小盒子，另一个双手捂着嘴。
# en: Open it now
opt.left.label [a90872] = 现在就打开
# en: Inside: a pebble from the lakeshore where you first really talked, polished to a shine. "It's stupid," {npc} says. It isn't. You carry it everywhere, and spend the next day hunting for something half as good to give back.
opt.left.say.1 [920de2] = 里面是一颗湖边的鹅卵石，来自你们第一次真正谈心的那片湖岸，被打磨得闪闪发亮。“这很傻，”{npc}说。一点也不傻。你走到哪儿都带着它，第二天又跑遍各处，想找一件哪怕有它一半好的回礼。
# en: Give {them} yours first
opt.right.label [64f5f8] = 先把你的送给{them}
# en: You'd had the same idea. You both open your boxes at once. They're nearly the same gift. You laugh until the sun goes down.
opt.right.say.1 [7c250d] = 你们想到一块儿去了。你们同时打开盒子。两份礼物几乎一模一样。你们一直笑到太阳落山。
